extends /views/templates/layouts/_base

append variables
	- pagetitle = "Chart types | Bar"
	- pagedescription = "Bar charts in Tablechart: bars laid sideways, so long names fit on one line."

block content
	.lane
		.container
			.page-header
				h1 Bar
				p.lead Bars laid sideways, for long names.

	+section("Bar chart")
		p Each row of the table is a bar. The names are shown to the left of the bars, so a long name fits on one line.

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="bar")
				figcaption
					b Juice pressed by variety
					br
					span thousands of litres
				table
					tbody
						each row in [['Bramley seedling', '31.4'], ['Cox’s orange pippin', '27.8'], ['Egremont russet', '18.2'], ['Discovery', '12.6'], ['Worcester pearmain', '9.1']]
							tr(data-kind=row[2])
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]

	+section("Numbers")
		p If a bar is long enough, its number is shown inside it. If not, the number is shown after the bar.

	+section("Long names")
		p A name beside a bar takes at most 40% of the width of the chart. A longer name wraps onto more lines, and the chart gets taller if it needs to. To change the width, set #[code --tablechart-name-max], such as #[code 30%].
		p A long word is hyphenated if the page has a #[code lang] attribute, such as #[code lang="en"].

	+section("Grouped bars")
		p If the table has more than one value column, each row is a group, with one bar for each value column. The column headers are the names in the legend under the chart.

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="bar")
				figcaption
					b Apples sold by variety
					br
					span thousands
				table
					thead
						tr
							th Variety
							th 2022
							th 2026
					tbody
						each row in [['Elstar', '118', '131', false], ['Granny Johnson', '12', '45', 'granny'], ['Jonagold', '140', '135', false], ['Braeburn', '109', '121', false]]
							tr
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]
								td= row[2]

	+section("Stacked bars")
		p Add #[code data-chart-stack] to the figure. The values of a row are shown one after the other in one bar, the first value column on the left. The total of the row is after the bar.

		+chart
			figure(data-chart="bar" data-chart-stack)
				figcaption
					b Apples sold
					br
					span thousands
				table
					thead
						tr
							th Variety
							th Farm shop
							th Market
					tbody
						each row in [['Elstar', '64', '38'], ['Granny Johnson', '12', '21'], ['Jonagold', '71', '45'], ['Braeburn', '52', '30']]
							tr
								th= row[0]
								td= row[1]
								td= row[2]

		p A number is shown inside its part of the bar if it fits. If not, it is left out. If you point at the row, or tap it, the numbers of that row are shown.

	+section("Next")
		p For short names, a #[a(href=url('/types/column.html')) column chart] uses less height.
